course: dictionary
lesson: 8021
title: Reflection: a picture, a bounce or a thought
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «A budgie staring at itself in a mirror may treat the reflection like another bird.» Here the reflection is the picture the budgie sees in the mirror.
explain: «Birds crash into windows because they see reflected trees and sky.» Reflected means bounced back. The trees and sky are not really behind the glass. The light is bouncing back off the window, so the birds see a copy of the outside world and fly into it.
explain: In maths, a reflection is a flip over a line, like a mirror line. In school, you may also be asked to write a reflection, which means careful thinking about what you learned. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
fact: A reflection is the picture you see in a mirror, in water or on a shiny surface.
fact: In science, reflection is light, sound or heat bouncing back off a surface.
fact: Smooth, shiny surfaces reflect best.
fact: In maths, a reflection flips a shape over a mirror line, so it looks like its mirror image.
fact: «On reflection» means after careful thought, and it is a useful phrase to use in your writing.
exercise: «Birds crash into windows because they see reflected trees and sky.» What does reflection mean here? | A careful think about the birds | *Light bouncing back off the glass | A picture of a bird on a wall | A flip of a shape over a line
exercise: In maths, what is a reflection? | A shape with equal sides | *A flip of a shape over a line, so it looks like its mirror image | A shape that spins around a point | A shape that slides to a new place
exercise: «A budgie staring at itself in a mirror may treat the reflection like another bird.» What is the reflection? | *The picture the budgie sees in the mirror | A window | A type of mirror | A real bird that lives in the room
test: In science, what is reflection? | *Light, sound or heat bouncing back off a surface | Light being made from nothing | A sound that stops suddenly | A picture of a shape on paper
test: What does «on reflection» mean? | A shiny surface | A flip over a line | *After careful thought about something | A picture in water
exam: Which surface reflects light best? | *Smooth and shiny | Soft and fluffy | Rough and bumpy | Dull and dark
